cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  complexplorer: visualization of complex functions, from phase portraits to
  3D-printable ornaments
message: If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Igor
    family-names: Kuvychko
    email: igor.kuvychko@gmail.com
repository-code: https://github.com/kuvychko/complexplorer
url: https://kuvychko.github.io/complexplorer/
abstract: >-
  Complexplorer renders complex functions as phase portraits, 3D analytic
  landscapes, Riemann spheres and Riemann surfaces, and exports modulus-scaled
  Riemann relief ornaments as STL for 3D printing. Inspired by Elias Wegert's
  "Visual Complex Functions - An Introduction with Phase Portraits".
keywords:
  - complex analysis
  - visualization
  - phase portrait
  - Riemann sphere
  - Riemann surface
  - domain coloring
  - 3D printing
license: MIT
version: 3.0.0
# Set to the release date when the tag is cut; see CONTRIBUTING.md, "Releasing".
date-released: 2026-09-19
